<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Tarred_Solvents.xml               UtinniPatches — SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1

  Item spec §3, "Solvents — a WEAK solvent craftable in-biome (an ACID
  rendered from thrummel seepwax, ruled generous per the item's own 'one
  raid should give you a lot' note); the cleaning mechanism is tar->green-
  gas reaction (cross-refs SUMP_GASLIGHT_1's verbatim rulings). Do NOT
  build the foreign STRONG-solvent trade side — just leave a def/trade-tag
  placeholder hook."

  PARTIAL BY DESIGN, three pieces:

  1. RUT_ThrummelSeepwax — the raw feedstock. sump_fauna_roster_2026-09-24.md
     §4 already names "seepwax" as the thrummel hive's own invented product
     (no donor def, chitin+wax economy, roster line 78). The thrummel
     creature/hive itself is NOT built this pass (0 of the roster's under-
     layer species exist yet, per that roster's own build-status table) — so
     this def carries NO recipeMaker (nothing to render it FROM yet) and is
     flagged as awaiting its real source, the hive raid, "ruled generous:
     one raid should give you a lot" (SUMP_GASLIGHT_1's own verbatim owner
     quote). Tradeable/debug-spawnable in the meantime, same "compiles now,
     real source owed" posture this whole kit already uses throughout
     (RUT_WickStem's own header is the precedent for "non-zero MarketValue
     only so the def is legally tradeable, not a pricing call").

  2. RUT_WeakTarSolvent — the local acid. Crafted straight from
     RUT_ThrummelSeepwax via recipeMaker (the SAME short vanilla route
     RM_SapResin -> RM_ToxinSealant already uses in this repo,
     Greentide/RM_Greentide_Items.xml — no separate RecipeDef needed for a
     plain bench-crafted resource). Deliberately GENEROUS yield
     (productCount 4 off a costList of 1) per the ruling's own "not meant as
     a starvation mechanic" — this is what actually cures RUT_Tarred
     (RUT_Tarred_Surgery.xml, this item's piece 2/3 seam) and gates vault
     extraction (SUMP_TAR_VAULT_1) and the gaslight reaction
     (SUMP_GASLIGHT_1) elsewhere.

     🔴 NOT BUILT THIS PASS: the tar->green-gas reaction chemistry itself.
     SUMP_GASLIGHT_1 owns "cleaning works BY the tar->green-gas reaction" as
     its own full mechanism (a Helixien-compatible gas byproduct, the
     warbling light, vault extraction, three uses of one acid) — this item's
     own verify section only promises "a weak solvent removes it [the
     hediff]", which RUT_Tarred_Surgery.xml's Recipe_RemoveHediff bill
     delivers directly, with no gas byproduct modeled here. Building the
     reaction/byproduct here would duplicate SUMP_GASLIGHT_1's own scope
     rather than extend it.

  3. RUT_StrongTarSolvent — the foreign trade hook ONLY, per this item's own
     explicit instruction not to build that side. No recipeMaker (never
     craftable here), no source def wired to it — a real, legally-tradeable
     ThingDef that BIOME_NUISANCE_NORMALIZATION_1's own Poison Forest acid
     line can later point trade routes at. Distinguished from the weak
     solvent by color/MarketValue only; both accepted as equally valid
     ingredients by RUT_Tarred_Surgery.xml's own ingredient filter (either
     cures the hediff; the strong one is simply never the thing a Sump
     colony can make for itself).

  Textures: a first draft reused vanilla Jade/Chemfuel texPaths as
  placeholders (the same reuse RUT_TarMoat.xml/RUT_WickStem.xml use
  elsewhere in this mod) — but validate_patch.py refused all three as a hard
  ERROR: UtinniPatches already ships its OWN art under
  Textures/Things/Item/Resource/ (RUT_Greenwood.png, RUT_Hardwood.png), so
  that folder is this mod's own claimed namespace, same trap RM_Filth_Tar.xml
  already hit for Textures/Things/Filth/. Repointed to three new RUT_-named
  folders (Graphic_StackCount is a Graphic_Collection subclass too —
  texPath is a FOLDER, confirmed against Verse/Graphic_Collection.cs, same
  finding RM_Filth_Tar.xml's header already made for Graphic_Cluster) with
  simple procedurally-drawn placeholder chunk icons, same posture as that
  def's own art. Real (hand-authored, reviewed) art is still owed.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_ThrummelSeepwax</defName>
    <label>thrummel seepwax</label>
    <description>Warm, waxy secretion harvested from a thrummel mound — the hive's own building material and, rendered right, the feedstock for the Sump's one homegrown acid. A raid on a mound yields it by the barrel; nothing about gathering it is stingy.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_ThrummelSeepwax</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(196, 156, 64)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>1.4</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.18</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>2</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>150</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_WeakTarSolvent</defName>
    <label>weak tar solvent</label>
    <description>Thrummel seepwax rendered down into a mild acid — sharp-smelling, safe enough to handle bare-handed, and the only thing on the Sump that lets go of tar once it has set. A colony that raids the mounds is never really short of it.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_WeakTarSolvent</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(178, 196, 110)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>2.2</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.2</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.3</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>3</DeteriorationRate>
      <WorkToMake>150</WorkToMake>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>100</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <recipeMaker>
      <recipeUsers>
        <li>TableMachining</li>
      </recipeUsers>
      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
      <displayPriority>420</displayPriority>
      <!-- Generous on purpose (owner ruling, SUMP_GASLIGHT_1: "one raid
           should give you a lot. Not meant as a starvation mechanism.") —
           4 solvent off 1 seepwax, not a 1:1 render. -->
      <productCount>4</productCount>
    </recipeMaker>
    <costList>
      <RUT_ThrummelSeepwax>1</RUT_ThrummelSeepwax>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- The foreign side — hook only, per this item's own instruction. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_StrongTarSolvent</defName>
    <label>strong tar solvent</label>
    <description>An industrial-strength acid, far past anything the Sump renders for itself — this is the Poison Forest's own line of work, not the tar-country trade the local mounds support. Whatever it touches lets go of tar at once, no scrubbing needed.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_StrongTarSolvent</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(214, 96, 48)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>7</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.2</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>3</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>RM_ForeignSolventTrade</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <!-- Deliberately no <recipeMaker> — never craftable here. Not wired to
         any trade route, caravan offer or faction stock this pass; the
         tradeTags entry above is the hook BIOME_NUISANCE_NORMALIZATION_1's
         Poison Forest pass wires up, not a working trade path yet. -->
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
